=== Generated Answer (model draft; check against evidence) ===
This paper explores domains in extractive text summarization by extending the conventional definition of "domain" from document categories into data sources, i.e., news publications [10]. The authors demonstrate that news publications can cause data distribution differences, which means publications themselves can also be defined as domains [3].

Before this extension, domains in the paper's context were document categories: among the existing datasets, only DUC and NYT are annotated with document categories, and DUC is designed only for competition testing [11]. An example of such category-based domains is "Dining and Wine" in NYT, which corresponds to "Food and Drink" in DUC 2002 [8].
